# Intentionally minimal — no `legacy-peer-deps` here.
#
# This file used to carry `legacy-peer-deps=true`, attributed to "React 18
# with Radix/RHF/etc. peer-deps". That attribution was wrong. A strict
# resolve (`npm install --no-legacy-peer-deps`) surfaces exactly one
# conflict, and React is not in it:
#
#   Found: zod@3.25.76   (root project, @novu/api and
#                         eslint-plugin-react-hooks all accept ^3 || ^4)
#   Could not resolve: peerOptional zod@^4.0.0 from better-call@1.3.5
#                      ↳ peer of @better-auth/core and @better-auth/sso
#
# One transitive package wants zod v4 while the app is on v3. That is now
# pinned explicitly by the `overrides` block in package.json rather than by
# disabling peer resolution across the whole tree — so a genuinely bad
# conflict elsewhere still fails loudly instead of being silently accepted.
#
# The override goes away when the app moves to zod v4. That is a breaking
# migration (`.errors` → `.issues`, changed string validators, different
# superRefine semantics) touching schemas/, the API route validators and
# lib/fetch-helpers.ts — a real project, not a version bump.
